      "discriminative_explanation": "The claim states the folding is the 'same operation.' The observations support this by showing a consistent geometric logic across different subjects: img-k7-o1 describes folds that are 'arranged vertically on one side and cross over,' while img-v9-o0 describes 'vertical, parallel folds' descending from the top. Crucially, img-q2-o4 notes that floral elements at the crown are 'integrated into a solid material... given their fixed forms.' The fact that distinct elements like flowers (v9-o4) and hair/veils (k7-o0, v9-o0) share the same rigid, carved geometric properties as the face suggests a single method of creation (carving/blocking in) rather than applied or variable techniques.",
